  "texts": {
    "preamble": "K.B.Rasheed vs The Food Safety Officer on 27 May, 2025 Author: P.V.Kunhikrishnan Bench: P.V.Kunhikrishnan Wp(C) No. 1260 Of 2021 2025:Ker:37071 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice P.V.Kunhikrishnan Tuesday, The 27Th Day Of May 2025 / 6Th Jyaishta, 1947 Wp(C) No. 1260 Of 2021 Petitioner/S: 1 K.B.Rasheed Aged 1 Years S/O. Basheer, Kerala Stores, 10/175 Market Road, Thodupuzha, Kompanaparambil, Karikoodu, Thodupuzha 2 George Sebastian, S/O. V.J.Varkey, Manatt, Athirampuzha P.O., Kottayam Dist., Pin-686 562 3 Periya Peak Tea Estates Pvt Ltd Periya P.O., Wayanad, Kerala-670 644 By Advs. George Mathews Sri.Pranoy K.Kottaram Sri.T.K.Sreenarayana Das Respondent/S: 1 The Food Safety Officer Thodupuzha Circle, Thodupuzha Dist., Pin-685 584 2 The Asst.Commissioner Of Food Safety, K.B.Rasheed vs The Food Safety Officer on 27 May, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/84147452/ 1 Designated Officer Of The Asst, Commissioner Of Good Safety) Idukki, Thodupuzha-685 584 Wp(C) No. 1260 Of 2021 2025:Ker:37071 By Advs. Addl.Director General Of Prosecution Shri.P.Narayanan, Addl.Public Prosecutor Director General Of Prosecution Smt.Seetha Sr.Pp This Writ Petition (Civil) Having Come Up For Admission On 27.05.2025, The Court On The Same Day Delivered The Following: Wp(C) No. 1260 Of 2021 2025:Ker:37071 P.V.Kunhikrishnan, J -------------------------------------- W.P. (C) No. 1260 of 2021 -------------------------------------- Dated this the 27th day of May, 2025 Judgment",
    "facts": "[sic] 2. The petitioners are aggrieved by Ext.P5 complaint filed by the 1st respondent, which was an adjudication initiated under Sec.3.1(z)(x) of the Food Safety and Standard Act r/w Regulation K.B.Rasheed vs The Food Safety Officer on 27 May, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/84147452/ 2 No.2.10.1 of Food Safety and Standards (Food Product Standards and Food Additives) Regulations, 2011 WP(C) NO. 1260 OF 2021 2025:KER:37071 on the allegation that they have manufactured and sold sub standard produce (Tea). In Ext.P1 analyst report, the only defect was that the sample contained extraneous matter (iron filings) above the permissible limit is the submission. In Ext.P6, the referral laboratory reversed the said finding is the submission. Therefore, there is divergent finding in the analyst report and the report of the referral laboratory.",
    "arguments": "Therefore, in the light of the dictum laid down by this Court in Pepsico India Holdings Private Limited v. State of Kerala and anr. [2024(6) KHC 251], the proceedings is unsustainable, is the submission. 3. This Court in Pepsico India's case (supra) observed like this : WP(C) NO. 1260 OF 2021 2025:KER:37071 \"15.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Therefore, in the light of the dictum laid down by this Court in Pepsico India Holdings Private Limited v. State of Kerala and anr. [2024(6) KHC 251], the proceedings is unsustainable, is the submission. 3. This Court in Pepsico India's case (supra) observed like this : WP(C) NO. 1260 OF 2021 2025:KER:37071 \"15."
